														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1658113">
									

<p>I'm kind of wondering why this isn't an EX-SCP. Sure, it's unheard of, but isn't it scientifically explainable? The venom is a liquid that undergoes an extreme endothermic reaction on contact with the air, and there are other creatures that can survive being frozen with no ill effects (i.e. cockroaches, tardigrades).</p>
<p>I guess I'm saying that the only really anomalous thing about this SCP is that it doesn't seem to have come from any sort of evolutionary progression - that it seems to have just come out of nowhere; and while all the genetic mutations it would take to make this kind of tarantula happening all at once in one embryo is extremely unlikely, it's not quite <em>impossible</em>, is it? If it's completely scientifically explainable, it's not an SCP…right? Am I missing something here?</p>

							</div>

								
